{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1384773-bikeshedding-a-condition","id":1384773,"title":"Bikeshedding a Condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-29T22:12:24-07:00","id":1384773,"title":"Bikeshedding a Condition","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Twould be a good thing to clean up the language on this and make it more consise. The idea, though, I think is pretty clear. Let me know if you think otherwise. It's a Condition to represent being aware of too much happening at once.</span></span><br /> <br /> Prismatic Soul (Condition)</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">A being with this Condition perceives ephemeral things alongside physical things, simultaneously. The effect appears similar to schizophrenia, except the scenes and senses being presented to their senses are demonstrable parts of reality, just not limited to <i>physical</i> reality. The difficulty is that this condition comes with no particular guidance about what is being viewed at any given time, and, in fact, doesn\u2019t usually discriminate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Ephemera intrude into the senses of such a person even without any special connection or place. The senses include impressions from multiple realms at once, which is disorienting, even when one becomes accustomed to the Condition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">These visions are distracting, imposing a -1 distraction penalty on any non-reflexive action and on any sensory tests, reflexive or otherwise. The uncertain nature of the ephemeral senses imposes a -3 penalty due to the haziness of the sense on top of that -1 for distraction. The hazy images of other realms are patchy and indistinct, but are not clear enough to trigger the Split Focus Tilt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Some particular visions snap into greater focus, generally when interacting with something. Anything not focused upon becomes harder to witness, suffering a -4 distraction penalty. The physical senses remain, but the realm or realms that hold attention gain full clarity, overwhelming the capacity of a human mind to properly handle it all, imposing the Split Focus Tilt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The subject can spend a point of Willpower and then roll current Willpower as a die pool. (include the willpower spent to activate this in the die pool) Success indicates that the senses can be consciously willed to focus on a specific phenomenon witnessed or to defocus if already snapped in.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Perhaps there is a similar but less severe Condition that deals with only one realm intruding at a time.)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Effects that externalize and direct one\u2019s ephemeral senses, such as astral projection or an astral journey, have an unusual effect on Prism Souls. Where these normally dislocate a mind and its frame of reference, the Prism Souled merely shift their ephemeral senses. Their waking mind and physical senses are otherwise unaffected.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">A dramatic success on meditation can quiet the ephemeral side if it focuses on a visualization of self and being in the moment. This removes the Split Focus Tilt and removes the normal distraction penalties.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This Condition interacts with quite a few merits. The following list is just a set of examples.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Astral Adept: The merit can be developed to use the connection from focusing on an astral object, removing the need for a ceremony or ritual to engage the ability.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Unseen Sense: If the Unseen Sense is towards a type of ephemera, that type of focused vision is triggered without a roll or willpower cost when something interesting of that sort occurs in sensory range. Neither a roll nor a willpower are required in such a case. If the user simply wishes to view that sort of phenomenon, that\u2019s now allowed a roll as normal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Medium: Contact almost always counts as a triggering event for the focusing vision.</span></span><br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Ecstatic Wind branding, Taking soul shock or degeneration in a verge, traumatic Awakening</span></span><br /> <b>Resolution:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Removing sensitivity to other worlds, patching the soul wound that caused the perception, The Lie blinding the subject</span></span><br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"color:#000000\">Updated version for consideration:<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamwalker (Condition)</b><br /> <br /> A being with this condition is sensitive to the resonance of the unseen things of creation. In particular, they are sensitive to things connected to their personal ancestry and the dream of the local area. Ephemera related to their ancestral history can make themselves known to the Dreamwalker's senses. The trouble with this is it becomes difficult to distinguish what comes from where when different aspects of reality collide. <br /> <br /> One's personal dreaming ancestry sets the things that are revealed to this sense readily. Anything resonant with the personal dreaming is unveiled. If the character is following a Songline, the sacred sites along the path also similarly shine through. This includes spirits, ghosts, or other phenomena resonant with the persona dream or the dream of the Songline being followed. Things that are resonant and not magically concealed are visible to the Dreamwalker. Things that are not resonant are generally invisible as normal, but a partial resonance can sometimes make flicker into visibility, especially if they attempt to interact.<br /> <br /> A -1 penalty is applied to rolls involving perception or penalized by distraction due to the various images that flit in and out of awareness rather frequently. If multiple forms apply, the penalty rises to -3.<br /> <br /> At an Iris that is resonant with the Dreamwalker's personal dreaming or current Songline, the Dreamwalker is drawn in automatically through the portal, provided they fulfill the entry requirements. Many Irises have this Condition as a valid alternate Key. A willpower can be spent to resist the pull. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Beats:</b> Take a beat every time you live out or learn the lesson of an ancestor's vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> There are only 3 ways to regain control of one's mind. One may reject their personal dream, complete its path, or transcend its limitations.<br /> <br /> To overcome the condition requires breaking ties with the personal dram in some dramatic way, generally defiling sacred sites or destroying some symbolic and irreplaceable (from a personal standpoint) token of the dream. <br /> <br /> Harmonizing with it requires one to follow the entire Song, visiting and honoring its sacred sites until all lessons are learned. Once the mage leaves the last test site, the visions cease.<br /> <br /> Those possessing deeper insight may seek to shape their dream, rather than merely follow it. At the final site, they meditate on the lessons learned, and gain insight into their Condition. The Dreamwalker Condition actually expands, in this case, permitting the Dreamwalker to focus attention on another and connect to their Dream. This resolution grants the Sleepwalker merit, if the character is not already considered one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-12-2020, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T03:34:20-07:00","id":1384817,"title":"","content":"This Condition is extremely over-engineered, imo. The basic effect is that the character is distracted, so have a flat and simple penalty for being distracted (perhaps -3 for actions that can be influenced by distractions, and -5 on rolls based on perception). If you want to allow the character to ignore the distractions, a Willpower point should do it without a roll. Rolling current Willpower points is not a mechanic that is used except for Soul-Shocked, and then it's because it directly deals with your number of Willpower points. Removing the roll means the player doesn't risk wasting a WP when they could've just spent it on +3 dice to partially or completely negate the penalty without any risk.<br /> Instead of focusing on a single thing, I recommend removing all distraction penalties for a turn or a number of turns equal to Composure.<br /> <br /> For a similar Condition applying only to the Shadow, check out Mystified in Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-30-2020, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:45:57-07:00","id":1385012,"title":"","content":"The point was to have some sporadic things called into focus from time to time but not predictably. A fixed blanket penalty doesn't <i>quite</i> work, but I appreciate the thoughts. I'll let it percolate a bit.<br /> <br /> I'll go check Mystified That might have some useful stuff to crib. (Ed. Hmm. Not really the same idea, but that variable penalty based on ambient conditions might be something to consider.)<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> <br /> Hmm: What about<b></b>: <br /> <br /> The general perception penalty is -1 physical and -3 ephemeral (any) <br /> No roll is required for something to snap into focus on its own, and that allows a reflexive perception roll without penalty. Any conscious examination would just have the penalty.<br /> <br /> When witnessing multiple types of ephemera in a round, throw in a distraction penalty of a die per type for the rest of the round and the next. An Instant mental action can sort things out to negate the distraction penalty and reduce the perception penalties by 1 for the same period.<br /> (Maybe just a distraction penalty if you use the reflexive examination)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-01-2020, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:05:45-07:00","id":1385039,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d treat it similarly to Postcognition personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:09:44-07:00","id":1385171,"title":"","content":"This seems like it needs to be broken down into several conditions. The ones currently present:<br /> <br /> - Minor hallucinations of a frequency of Twilight: -1 penalty<br /> <br /> - Partial projection of senses into a superimposing Realm Invisible, similar to how werewolves split their senses: -3 penalty<br /> <br /> - Forced projection of senses into a superimposing Realm Invisible, which can be fought off with Willpower: -4 penalty and Split Focus tilt<br /> <br /> All of them resolved via an exceptional success in a meditation roll.<br /> <br /> Because these can stack, they seem like they could be crippling to a target without high mental attributes. I think they are lacking a trigger or suppression mechanism, so the character can pursue a cure while maintaining a fascinating level of weirdness. These seem like the kind of troubles prospective Dreamspeakers are said to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T22:22:01-07:00","id":1385192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1384773-bikeshedding-a-condition?p=1385171#post1385171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These seem like the kind of troubles prospective Dreamspeakers are said to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You caught me...<br /> <br /> I was writing up a 2e Dreamspeaker legacy that works by taming a crippling persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> edit: So I peeked at Werewolf again, since you made a good point. A -2 to perception and rolls where distraction plays a roll works pretty well for a single realm conflating. To keep things simple, the background version could be simplified down to the same penalty due to transient noise from the various planes providing a -1 and a cumulative -1 could be assessed for each focused form of vision in play.<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to think of a clean approach to triggering the visions.I was originally thinking along the lines of &quot;if the ephemera interacted in any way, even just feeding on essence generated by the character, the vision triggers&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would love to come up with something clever that helps guide a bit more than &quot;just narrate that wackiness&quot;.I'd kinda like to work it so the beats rewards a good embrace of the weirdness without derailing all plot/other players and without making it an overly handy merit.The penalties should help with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-04-2020, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:19:06-07:00","id":1385938,"title":"","content":"Since the inspiration for the Dreamspeakers is Australian Aboriginal mythology, you could lean into that. I also mixed the Gift of Men from the Silmarillion to define the resolution.<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: Songline</b><br /> <br /> By effort, chance or instinct, you have gained a connection to your Songline. Some call it the sacred narrative of creation, where it is said one's entire ancestry exists as one and their sum knowledge is accumulated. Legend has it the most ancient ones traveled across the land before the Fall, creating sacred sites in their journeys. These living tales come to the mage to be passed on.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the human mind has long forgotten how to understand them. The mage has automatic perception and can physically interact with the Mind or Spirit attuned Twilight of a region that is resonant with his Songline's ancestors or symbolism (like a specialized variation of Shadow Name). These images overlap with the material, applying a -2 to perception rolls. <br /> <br /> When more than one Twilight is resonant, this penalty becomes -3 instead as the mage's mind struggles to differentiate each phase of reality. However, this is usually a portent indicating an important locale in their Songline.<br /> <br /> In resonant Loci or Synesne, the mage is drawn into the Realm Invisible immediately, but can spend a Willpower per turn to resist the pull.<br /> <br /> <b>Beats:</b> Take a beat every time you live out or learn the lesson of an ancestor's vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> There are only 3 ways to regain control of one's mind. One may defy the Song, harmonize with it or move beyond it. <br /> <br /> Defying it is the path of the Banisher and it requires one to destroy or defile all sacred sites they can currently perceive in their Song, thus severing the sympathetic connection.<br /> <br /> Harmonizing with it requires one to follow the entire Song, visiting and honoring its sacred sites until all lessons are learned. Once the mage leaves the last test site, the visions cease.<br /> <br /> Those possesing deeper insight may seek to corroborate their right to shape the melody rather than just listen to it. At the final site, they meditate on the fresh enlightenment before leaving, following the Songline in their soul deep into the Dreamtime. There they will face the final trial of the Dreamtime entity representing their Song. Those that pass return with the authority to speak for the Dreamer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-05-2020, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:26:23-07:00","id":1385968,"title":"","content":"Well, I certainly like it better, but it still needs something. This doesn't quite have the crazed edge I was hoping for, but it <i>does</i> have better rules for the general wackiness. It's close to ready for prime time.<br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose I'll toss out some further conversion notes and see what you think:<br /> <br /> Dreamborn is a subtype of supernal entity, more or less, that have Arcana of the sorts of things goetia and spirits have Influences over. There are a couple other quirks, like the fact that they are connected to lesser representations of them in various realms, regardless of type. (Luna is a Dreamborn. Her Spirit and her Geotia representations are simply parts of her by this reckoning.) They can be summoned by magi of any Path, but their preference in that matter weighs in heavily on the difficulty. There are two challenges, one is part of the summoning itself, which is often a quest. The other is imposed by the Dreamborn itself. Only the first is mandatory but they almost exclusively choose to require both.<br /> <br /> (I was intending to polish the dreamborn bit up next.)<br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dreamland (Merit: 1 dot)</b><br /> <br /> A Dreamland is a place of power that connects a site in the physical to a specific and stable astral location. This is usually Temenos but can be the Dreamtime. The site counts as a Synese to the Dreamland. These are always locked by a Key and the Key always includes a specific feature of the site that must be maintained or access is lost.<br /> <br /> The physical location of such sites is generally miles apart.<br /> <br /> Such sites have often been used for generations as storehouses of supernal wisdom. Uncovering how to access the information, however, is a Mystery that this merit does not represent solving. This merit specifically represents fairly certain access to such a site and access to the key. Safe Place, Library, and Advanced Library are often appropriate to represent unlocking the trove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T19:17:41-07:00","id":1385992,"title":"","content":"Because the Aborigenal traditions are transmitted orally, I think that could figure into the summoning of Dreamborn. There is a recent topic on other types of Grimmoires. So borrowing from that, you could say they can only be summoned by Seals. <br /> <br /> Dreamtime seals could be mental constructs and therefore can be acquired by many. They require the mage to pass their trial, this is the Mind component. Following the Songline gives the mage a part of the fractured Grimmoire of his associated Dreamborn. Once all the experiences are assembled in their mind, it becomes the Seal. <br /> <br /> Other ones can be found in sites of the Astral or Hisil, with all the varying complexity and danger associated with Grimmoire hunting.<br /> <br /> The summoning itself would require an additional Spirit component: enough Resonance to open the way.<br /> <br /> The Dreamtime itself could be found deep within the Anima Mundi, in a limiar place between the Shadow and Astral (a shortcut Reality Stalkers might like to use). <br /> <br /> I need to ponder more on the Dreamland merit. Right now the image that comes to mind is Dark Souls 2, using the Ashen Mist Heart to dive into the memories of the giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-05-2020, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T18:16:21-07:00","id":1386220,"title":"","content":"I figured some of these ideas can be unified. <br /> <br /> The key to opening a dreamland might be a simple action or material thing, but the key to actually unlocking the secret teachings or moving beyond it into the rest of the Inner Realms might require having one of that same sort of seals. The paths unlocked by these places may well lead to other seals, as well. (I lean towards the merit representing the beginning of a mystery and access to it.)<br /> <br /> Of course, some of the seals could be items torn from the dreamborn by ancient heroes. Others could be gifts traded for. <br /> <br /> It occurred to me that learning enough about a dreamborn to earn the right to call on it might require interaction with multiple of its avatars. I'll have to reread the Signs passage on Mysteries and see if I can work out a system to use for this.<br /> <br /> I was originally thinking of tweaking the normal supernal summoning rules, but... What if it's an extended social contest: Open enough Doors and the dreamborn deigns to show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:03:18-07:00","id":1386388,"title":"","content":"Yep, that was direction I imagined the Seals could guide them in. In general I was thinking that this condition:<br /> <br /> * Teaches intuitive knowledge that they can follow up on after obtaining the Legacy.<br /> <br /> * Is very inconvenient without being fully crippling. If your Songline's area has a Twilight that places you in the trenches of a WW1 battlefield your ancestor fought in, then you have a problem. You will look afraid, dock behind furniture and speak of things that aren't there for those without the perceptions. So that pressures them to find a cure.<br /> <br /> * Is logically consistent from an inside look. One of my favorite things about Werewolf is how there is a clear way for the lupines to maintain a balanced Harmony. It makes sense to them, but to the uninitiated it looks like a fierce, violent and alien mentality, unless they manage it discreetly.<br /> <br /> The avatars being able to also grant the Seals or part of them sounds very thematic. I think apart from Signs, the Summoners book could provide some ideas, alongside their original writeup in Legacies:The Ancient. Perhaps the Astral Realms book might also have some information on Dreamborn.<br /> <br /> The summoning via social interaction sounds like a cool third Attainment, something that could earn them their name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:55:17-07:00","id":1387150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1384773-bikeshedding-a-condition?p=1386388#post1386388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The summoning via social interaction sounds like a cool third Attainment, something that could earn them their name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Yeah, that's exactly where I was tossing it. I debated 4, but that seemed too late.<br /> <br /> <br /> Clearly, the only thing we differ on is the &quot;inconvenient without being crippling&quot; notion. I prefer it as sporadically crippling and generally minor*. (A bit like PTSD) That explains what you did, though, and I agree that it served that purpose.<br /> <br /> (*ed. &quot;generally minor&quot; in the sense of most of the time, it's not causing heart racing or flashbacks)<br /> <br /> Heck, I might be persuaded, yet. I'm softening.<br /> <br /> ed. You know what, I'm sold. When interacting with the visions, it's sufficiently wyrd and disconcerting. When you talk about resonant to the songline, that covers a few different issues. In fact, I will probably tweak my Dreamspeaker write up to incorporate that in the attainments: I might change the projecting into ephemeral realms thing into the ability to shape their Songline's resonance. It wouldn't quite be as fluid as simply going wherever you want, and I actually like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> You know: If we can work out a solid ephemeral summoning system based on social conflict and ritual preparation, I bet it could find some use in other splats, even, not merely elsewhere in Mage. I'll have to review the various systems and trawl for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-09-2020, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:44:35-07:00","id":1387157,"title":"","content":"Cool, glad you liked it. I got that idea from reading about their real world culture, even the name. <br /> <br /> Making a social maneuvering summoning system reusable by other splats seems very cool.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Dreamspeakers themselves,<br /> here is a rough idea for it:<br /> <br /> First impression levels could be the lesser of [Mind] and [Spirit].<br /> <br /> Because its a targeted summoning, its safe from Abyssal incursion.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what you summon, you need a Seal to use this Attainment.<br /> <br /> The rules for the target number of succeses remain the same, but they are now Doors to be opened. Negotiating conditions can open them as normal. <br /> <br /> I imagine this would happen in a dreamscape, allowing them to even negotiate parts of their mind if necessary. <br /> <br /> Lastly, negotiations do not free the summoner from the entity's trial.<br /> <br /> So in theory they can summon extremely quickly, but they need to do their research and be very diplomatic to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-09-2020, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T16:01:35-07:00","id":1387610,"title":"","content":"I'm not finding anything about songlines when I'm looking up Australian aboriginal belief (Found great stories that fit perfectly, of course.) Any good titles or links would be welcome. I don't know as much as I'd prefer about their world view.<br /> <br /> Be nice to use their myth to guide the factors for the summoning and the songline ideas. I was working off of the assumption that Dreamspeakers have a huge advantage in gaining the prerequisite knowledge for calling on the Dreamborn and likely have some blood ties that make things easier, too, due to lineage. Otherwise, though, I figure they aren't a whole lot better at the summoning part than other folks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Minor aside:<br /> I don't think &quot;Seal&quot; is quite the right term for the attainment of secret wisdom.I think it works better as the term for a discrete point in the songline that prohibits progress until mastered. If Songlines are Mysteries with Locked Opacity, Seals are its Key Mysteries, I would think. That makes a little more sense to me, from a linguistic standpoint. Something more like &quot;token&quot; seems better for the thing the seeker needs to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My current thoughts on the summoning process:<br /> <br /> 1. Learning: Who are you trying to call? You need to figure out who they are to properly call on them. Their name is required, and it must be a real name. Many hide behind masks and false names..You also need to understand what they are. A token representing their nature is required, later on, that might be uncovered in this phase. This is largely a mental phase.<br /> <br /> 2. Rights: Dreamborn are sapient entities with goals and prejudices. There are fundamental laws governing their interactions and then there are their own laws. Fundamental laws require a token representing the being in question and some sort of appropriate ritual to open up the conduit. The token must be a meaningful token gathered from a songline quest and the ritual requires personal effort, generally both physical and astral. If the Dreamborn considers the Seeker to have the right to call on them, such as if they are a descendant or adopted into their family, then that will help at the Appeal phase as one step up on the Impression chart. If the request is something promised by the Dreamborn or framed as an obligation that the Dreamborn accepts, multiple Doors would be opened.<br /> <br /> 3. Preparation: The area into which the entity is being called must be prepared with the tokens in a manner befitting the entity called. (Some vision quests prepare the seeker's Oneiros to the purpose. All?) This involves placing proper symbols around the meeting place and often involves music and fires. There are minimal requirements to be met to successfully create the conduit. Then there are things that are wise to include because the Dreamborn in question prefers them. Depending on how perfectly these details are met, this can raise or lower the impression by a step.<br /> <br /> Generally, an effigy of the being sought is set up as a symbol of the subject. Permanent effigies in the community (e.g. totem poles, churinga, shrines with statues) can often provide this to many generations of seekers.<br /> <br /> 4. Opening: The Seeker must perform the rite, expending the energy as required to create the conduit that opens the site to the Dreamborn.<br /> If the Dreamborn's name that is used is incorrect, this isn't selective and may be a bit insulting to the intended target. (Which might reduce Impression by a step) Other things may sneak in, in such a case. This is also possible if the Abyss sneaks into the summoning. (If possible)<br /> <br /> The rolls for this part of the rite is meditation. Success on this phase means that the conduit is formed, opening a path to the Dreamtime. Sufficient success (meditation must reach the Dreamtime) reduces the difficulty of the interaction on the part of the Dreamborn. An exceptional success makes interaction trivial, and so normally opens a Door automatically. This phase includes a difficult trial related to the nature of the dreamborn. Calling on Death, for example, requires the character face their fear of mortality to simply open the Conduit.<br /> <br /> 5. Appeal: The dreamborn is contacted, but that doesn't mean it cares.If this is the first contact the two have made, the Dreamborn's first impression of the character is affected by the performance in the Opening trial. At this point, the Dreamborn's personal challenge is faced. That's challenge is usually not specified in words, and, instead, comes in an astral trial of some sort. This takes place in the strange timeframe of the dreaming earth, so it takes a surprisingly short amount of time to those not participating. Failing the Dreamborn's challenge reduces the impression by a step. An average impression generally means that the Seeker gets one very brief shot at impressing the Dreamborn before it closes the Conduit forcibly. (That is, a single roll to attempt to improve the impression) If the impression ever becomes hostile, the Dreamborn will usually strike the Seeker down, shattering the conduit and flinging them back to their body in soul shock. Failing to improve an average impression can sometimes end this way, as well. If the challenge is failed and the Seeker returns home to try again later, the travel is as normal.<br /> <br /> 6. Treating: The Seeker has the attention of the dreamborn. Let Social Combat begin. Make your case to the strange ancient spirit.<br /> <br /> With this approach, the summoning actually <i>must</i> take place in multiple strata. Maybe even prepare and cast in each strata to create the conduit.<br /> <br /> (Hmm. Maybe replace &quot;conduit&quot; with &quot;trail&quot; or &quot;track&quot;? Serpent themes are pretty common in the stories I'm finding.)<br /> <br /> Teamwork should be able play a role in the summoning, if only as a sort of moral support and grabbing stuff you need.<br /> <br /> Rank should make things more difficult for a seeker, even if the Dreamborn is friendly, I think. Perhaps the trial of the conduit/trailblazing phase should have stages to overcome based on the Dreamborn's rank. Of course, if we make it too lopsided, it won't make sense. Maybe there is a penalty for blazing an insufficient trail that makes manifesting difficult and hampers deals, but if the Dreamborn deigns to, it might be able to manifest.<br /> <br /> (Alternately, <i>that</i> could be the point of the effigy: granting it easy manifestation or, at the very least, contact. It could be as simple as letting it know that they are fans to secure a slight Impression bonus, too, going the other way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-12-2020, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T19:25:47-07:00","id":1387629,"title":"","content":"I got the general idea from this article:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Blackheaded_python.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songline\" target=\"_blank\"> Songline - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songline\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songline </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Then I traced the references:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://japingkaaboriginalart.com/articles/songlines-important-aboriginal-art/\" target=\"_blank\">https://japingkaaboriginalart.com/ar...boriginal-art/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://japingkaaboriginalart.com/articles/connection-dreamtime-songlines/\" target=\"_blank\">https://japingkaaboriginalart.com/ar...ime-songlines/</a><br /> <br /> Breaking down the mechanics of the system, the Learning and Rights take more time, but grant more benefits.<br /> <br /> I think the Preparation takes the same time as readying for a summoning. Opening uses about half the time (30 minutes per meditation roll). But there is still a risk of Abyssal intrusions, so it seems less easy to use on the go than, for example, the 2ed conversion of the Choir of Hasmallim or Katsinam Suukya.<br /> <br /> The Appeal seems like a way to open diplomatic channels and may be bypassed when you already have a decent relationship with the being. It does add a risk with the trial.<br /> <br /> If that is successful, they have to win a Social Battle.<br /> <br /> So in essence:<br /> <br /> * Its not safe from Abyssal incursions <br /> * Takes the same kind of setup as normal summonings, but grants different benefits <br /> * The meditation takes half the time as normal summonings<br /> * You face two trials: the Appeal and the Social Battle<br /> <br /> Its very cool thematically, but mechanically it needs to incentivize using the Attainment over the normal system. Being able to summon faster, safer or both once the right setup was obtained.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it would be possible for them to take a mental snapshot of the area and capture the feel of an existing ritual space, allowing them to use it from their Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-12-2020, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T23:27:08-07:00","id":1387655,"title":"","content":"First, thanks. I probably should have started at Wiki... heh. I'll read through that stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing that it grants over Path summoning is that anybody can theoretically do it, provided a functional Songline for the quest. (which Mind should be able to unlock) Another is the more human mindset that they have.. especially the direct ancestors. Their Boons could be extremely valuable. (Tempted to suggest the WtF Totem merit as a fairly common Boon. Protection from something under their control or blessings that they can provide would all make some sense.)<br /> <br /> (Ed. Having read through some, I'm torn about describing the conduit/track as a songline or the songline as the preparation in the physical side. Walking a songline and performing the songs can be the ceremony appropriate to Astral Adept, after all.)<br /> <br /> If we suss out a solid system for it, I expect to find places that make sense to inject the Dreamspeaker bonuses.<br /> <br /> One obvious one is facility doing the homework. Another I've been considering is the ability to listen to and participate in other songlines. (I'll read more about them to decide if/how that makes sense)<br /> <br /> I think their theme of living in multiple worlds at once could make trailblazing for them easier. Maybe add in their Mind as bonus dice. (maybe even as automatic successes on the first roll)<br /> If carving a trail from physical to astral is normally a difficult part of their task, perhaps the Dreamspeaker's edge might actually be an ability to skip that step with automatic success, provided preparation was made correctly. (That fits the first roll gaining automatic successes, come to think)<br /> <br /> Trails in the real world fade if not maintained, so perhaps a system for these trails being stabilized by waypoints could be set up, making established paths still require trails, but aiding the preparation and meditation phases. That could be the basis of the Dreamworld phenomenon. They are beginnings of paths and might continue or their continuation has been allowed to fade.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, yeah: Treating with an entity once a good relationship (heck, even a mediocre one) is established would become much easier. You'd be starting off more or less at the previous impression and with any agreements as established, much as with any other NPC, really. That's what I was thinking by making it a social system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-12-2020, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}